# Flux

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before any change. It is the only rulebook, and it says what to
read next: `ROADMAP.md` for what to build, `docs/COURSE-STANDARD.md` for the bar and the exemplar
files, `docs/courses/<id>.md` for the course's spine, and `DECISIONS.md` for what is settled.

For a procedure, open and follow the matching `SKILL.md` in `.claude/skills/`:

- `flux-new-course`: start a course from its spine.
- `flux-build-unit`: build or rework one unit to the standard.
- `flux-review-unit`: self-review a unit before opening its PR.
- `flux-content-drop`: the weekly PHY 2049 content drop.

Do not add rules here. Change `AGENTS.md` instead, so Claude Code and Cursor read the same rules.
